# DEPRECATED: relaxed_runner.py

This runner has been deprecated in favor of the unified `unattended_runner.py`.

## Why deprecated

- Uses `uv run pytest` instead of `sys.executable -m pytest`
- Has OOP-style API incompatible with the authoritative runner
- Lacks the stage registry architecture required by the blueprint
- Test expectations (`GROUP_REGISTRY`, `run_group`, etc.) don't match implementation

## Replacement

Use `unattended_runner.py` which provides:
- Complete 6-stage registry (preflight, provider, integration, strategy, agent, regression)
- `shell=False` subprocess invocation
- Credential injection via `build_child_env()`
- Output redaction
- Structured `StageResult` returns
- Direct pytest invocation without external tools

## Migration

Old code:
```python
from relaxed_runner import RelaxedRunner
runner = RelaxedRunner(cred_file, log_dir)
results = runner.run_campaign(groups)
```

New code:
```python
from unattended_runner import run_stage, load_credentials
credentials = load_credentials(cred_file)
result = run_stage("provider", credentials)
```
